  +#### Missing Board
  +
  +- When the selected board is absent, use the owner, repository, theme title and originating proposal record when applicable.
  +
  +##### 1. Create Absent Proposals Board
  +
  +When [Selected Kind](#selected-kind) is proposals and no open board under [Board Owner](#board-owner) has the [proposals title](#proposals-board), Apply [Create Proposals Board](#create-proposals-board). The copy source and the title meet [Proposals](#proposals).
  +
  +##### 2. Create Absent Theme Board
  +
  +- When the selected theme board is absent:
  +- Use the owner, [repository](#repository), theme title and originating proposal record when applicable.
  +
  +- Require the originating proposal record in [Theme Provenance](#theme-provenance) for a proposal-derived board; provide a missing-input finding when its designator is unavailable.
  +
  +- Run [Find Board Template](#find-board-template) under [Board Owner](#board-owner) with the exact [theme-template title](#theme-boards).
  +
  +- Use the provided number as the copy source.
  +
  +- Run [Copy Board Template](#copy-board-template) with that template number, the owner and the title required by [One Board Per Theme](#one-board-per-theme).
  +
  +- Retain the new board number. The copy carries the [theme-board fields](#theme-boards).
  +
  +- Run [Link Board to Repository](#link-board-to-repository) with the owner, new board number and [repository](#repository).
  +
  +- Retain the [Copied Board](#copied-board) after linking succeeds.
  +- Require the new theme's label and board before an initiative takes that theme.
  +
  +##### 3. Retain Copied Board
  +
  +Retain the [Copied Board](#copied-board) after the selected creation path succeeds.
  +
  +#### Saved Board Delivery
  +
  +- After the issue bodies and closures are saved:
  +
  +##### 1. Read Current Delivery Evidence
  +
  +- Read the issues, the board and its delivery records.
  +- Apply [Read Tracker Issue](#read-tracker-issue) for the [Saved Identities](#saved-identities).
  +- Apply [Read Board State](#read-board-state) for the selected board.
  +- Apply [Fetch All Delivery Pull Requests](#fetch-all-delivery-pull-requests) for its repositories and items.
  +- Apply [Fetch Pull Request Issue Links](#fetch-pull-request-issue-links) for those records.
  +- Fetch the published agent review records linked from each open epic integration pull request, retaining absent or unreadable evidence as a handoff blocker.
  +- Apply [Read Board Configuration](#read-board-configuration).
  +- Run [Find User](#find-user).
  +- Retain these provided snapshots for the following computation.
  +
  +##### 2. Plan Delivery Changes
  +
  +- Run [Compute Board Changes](#compute-board-changes) to the captured evidence.
  +- Fetch each unresolved issue.
  +- Run [Compute Board Changes](#compute-board-changes) again, adding the fetched off-board issue records to the retained evidence.
  +
  +##### 3. Apply and Confirm Calls
  +
  +- Run each emitted call, including the assignee calls, which act on the issue rather than the board item.
  +- Apply [Read Board Configuration](#read-board-configuration) for each changed item to confirm its current status.
  +
  +- If that item still shows the preceding status:
  +- Repeat its emitted write call.
  +- Apply [Read Board Configuration](#read-board-configuration) again for the same item. The item list can lag a write.
  +
  +##### 4. Recompute Refreshed Board
  +
  +- Fetch the issues and items again.
  +- Refresh the pull request metadata and linked published agent review records before recomputing statuses; either tip may have changed during the writes.
  +- Run [Compute Board Changes](#compute-board-changes) to the refreshed evidence, retaining every resolved off-board issue record.
  +- Stop when it emits no further call and every changed item has been confirmed. An issue added in one pass gets its status in the next.
  +
  +##### 5. Retain Confirmed Board Statuses
  +
  +Retain [Confirmed Statuses](#confirmed-statuses) after every changed item has been confirmed, retaining any unresolved discrepancy.
