  +- Apply [Check Epic Readiness](#check-epic-readiness) against current delivery and verification evidence.
  +
  +- Reconcile the expected bases with the task delivery targets.
  +
  +- Confirm from [Base Merges](#base-merges) that every base has merged into its corresponding long-lived branch. An unknown or incomplete base list, or missing merge evidence, leaves completion unconfirmed even when every task is delivered and every criterion is ticked.
  +
  +- Retain the completion result in [Delivery State](#delivery-state), identifying remaining blockers. Passing normal delivery checks supplies the evidence for the closure step; the tracker issue's current Development-link gate still governs the write.
   
   #### Initiative Completion
   
   - For an initiative:
   - Apply [Read Tracker Issue](#read-tracker-issue) for every linked epic.
  -- Apply [Check Initiative Completion](#check-initiative-completion) with the current initiative JSON, all linked epic records, criterion verification evidence and captured Development-link and pull-request records.
  +- Use the current initiative JSON, all linked epic records, criterion verification evidence and captured Development links and pull requests.
  +
  +- Evaluate [Initiative Record](#initiative-record), [Epic Records](#epic-records), [Verification Evidence](#verification-evidence) and [Development Evidence](#development-evidence) against [Delivery State](#delivery-state).
  +
  +- Identify each missing, open or cancelled epic, each unverified or unticked criterion, and each unmerged or unreadable Development-linked pull request. Incomplete link evidence leaves completion unconfirmed.
  +
  +- Retain the completion result and its supporting issue identities, evidence revisions and blockers. Passing normal delivery checks supplies the caller's closure evidence; the tracker issue's current Development-link gate still governs the write.
   
   #### Completion Result
   
differing: skills/work-planner/protocols/issue-closure.md ### 4. Close
  --- skills/work-planner/protocols/issue-closure.md
